> Is there an official R repo for bleeding edge R?
>
> I mean I know this list is for getting R into F, but as a 'test bed'
> for early F/R yum adopters like us?

It generally isn't a big job to tweak R.spec to either apply
the R-patched diffs or to build a newer version of R.
For people who have R code to maintain it is nice to test
whenever a non-trivial patch appears rather than wait for
people to find problems when a new release arrives.

