From tcallawa at redhat.com  Mon Dec 22 21:21:28 2008
From: tcallawa at redhat.com (Tom Callaway)
Date: Mon, 22 Dec 2008 21:21:28 +0000
Subject: [Fedora-r-devel-list] R 2.8.1
Message-ID: <1229980888.4528.53.camel@localhost.localdomain>

R 2.8.1 is packaged up and queued up for testing. Please test this out:

Fedora 9:
https://admin.fedoraproject.org/updates/rpy-1.0.3-6.fc9,R-2.8.1-1.fc9
Fedora 10:
https://admin.fedoraproject.org/updates/rpy-1.0.3-6.fc10,R-2.8.1-1.fc10

Once you've tested it, please, please, go to the update URL above and
click "Add A Comment". If it works for you, click "Works for me" and
write a little bit about how you tested it. That counts as a "+1" of
karma for that update. When it gets to +3, the system automatically
flags the update to be pushed to stable.

You don't have to specifically test rpy to give karma on the update, I
have a high degree of confidence in rpy continuing to work. 

Thanks in advance,

~spot

